  <!--
    Seed data — all values from TOR §4.2, §4.4, §4.5.
    IDs are generated by the DB (gen_random_uuid() default on each column).
    FK references use name-based subqueries — no hardcoded UUIDs anywhere.
    Idempotency: each changeset is tagged runOnChange="false" (Liquibase default);
    re-running on a clean DB always produces a consistent state regardless of
    the generated UUID values.
  -->

  <!-- ================================================================
       CHANGESET 1: Device types (28 rows)
       Source: TOR §4.2 — deduplicated union of OS + PS + Video tables.
       Devices appearing in multiple systems get ONE device_type row.
  ================================================================ -->
